{
  "_comment": [
    "Example `<workdir>/crustify/artifacts/schedule.json`: the order of the campaign's",
    "modules, and its waves with their items and batches. `modules` lists them by `layer`:",
    "src/core.c comes first, and its use of src/io.c's widget_stream is cut. Planning",
    "appends waves after the highest index, and their `index` is their permanent id, not",
    "their position: `todo` waves run in the order of `depends_on.scheduled`, the lowest",
    "index first among those ready at once. A wave's `items` are planned; its `batches`",
    "are packed when it starts, and with `status` and `commits` record its progress. Each",
    "batch's id is wave-<index>/batch-<index>, which names its branch and worktree. A",
    "batch's task.json carries its kind as `objective`, its items, its batch fields and the",
    "run fields. Wave 1's first batch binds widget_stream, the cut dependency its",
    "widget_open needs, ahead of it, homed in src/io.c's file; wave 2 then finds it landed",
    "and packs only widget_read. Wave 0's batch 2 reviews its batches 0 and 1. Homes follow",
    "the coding conventions: src/<link-unit>/ in the campaign's own repository; C paths are",
    "below c/. An independent illustration: it is not a schedule for templates/modules.json.",
    "Each wave is one module's. src/io.c's `external` record names libz, whose z_stream_s its",
    "widget_stream holds: libz's side campaign wraps it, and no wave here does.",
    "Each planned item's release points are null in this wrap campaign, whose schedule binds the API; in a port campaign they place the later stages, `port/layout`, `port/memory` and `port/unexport`, each a planned item of its own with the stage as its objective."
  ],
